{
 "section_summary": "This section closes a Counter Intelligence Corps inquiry into the loyalty and repatriation of an American consular employee in Mukden. It then contains intelligence on Japanese secret societies in postwar China, a Tientsin despatch enclosing translated Japanese Gendarmerie records on Allied personnel and property, and the opening of a long report on Japanese naval intelligence in China. The naval report includes an eyewitness account of monitoring American radio traffic during the Leyte landings.",
